  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppComm 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'You notice that some patients in your community cannot afford a newly
    approved treatment option and/or are not being invited to participate in follow-up
    programs.


    <b>What impact does the community advocate have in this situation?</b>'
  explanation: Community advocates help raise awareness about access barriers and
    inequities that may affect certain groups. By speaking up, they encourage researchers
    and healthcare systems to consider ways to improve fairness and inclusion. This
    helps ensure that post-market monitoring reflects the full community, strengthening
    trust and supporting more equitable care.
  correctAnswer: Raising concerns about access and equity so all communities are
    considered
  incorrectAnswer1: Managing post-market research data and identifying patterns
  incorrectAnswer2: Updating insurance coverage rules for the newly approved treatment
  incorrectAnswer3: None of these answers
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Approval
